# =========================================================
# RANK 1 - "The good mug"
# GATE: char husband, rank 1, period evening, room living_room
# =========================================================

~ start

$> locals.tone = 0
$> GameState.location("Living room · Evening")
$> GameState.sprite("husband", "couch")

The film's been on for forty minutes. He hasn't looked at it once.

Eric: [#mood=neutral, #pose=couch] Long day.

Mom: [#mood=neutral, #pose=standing] They're all long.

He nods like that was a real answer. Then he reaches over and puts a mug on the side table in front of her.

Eric: [#mood=soft] The good one. Top shelf.

Mom: [#mood=surprised] You got the good mug out.

Eric: [#mood=soft] It's Tuesday.

Mom: [#mood=neutral] What's wrong with the other mugs.

Eric: [#mood=soft] Nothing. This one's better.

He goes back to not watching the film.

- Thank him properly.
	$> locals.tone += 1
	Mom: [#mood=soft] Thank you. Properly.
	Eric: [#mood=surprised] ...For a mug?
	Mom: [#mood=soft] For noticing I was tired.
	Eric: [#mood=averted] Huh.
- Say nothing. Drink it.
	Mom: [#mood=neutral] Mm.
	She drinks it. Still warm. He timed it.
- Ask why he's still up.
	Mom: [#mood=neutral] You're still up.
	Eric: [#mood=neutral] So are you.

The film ends. Neither of them watched it.

Eric: [#mood=neutral] Same time tomorrow?

Mom: [#mood=neutral] Same time tomorrow.

He takes both mugs through to the kitchen. She listens to him rinsing them.

Sixteen years. She has never once thought about what he does with the good mug.

if locals.tone >= 2
	$> GameState.apply("eric_r1_bonus")
else
	$> GameState.apply("eric_r1")

$> GameState.rank_card("husband", 1)

=> END